 "drivingQuestion": "What joins separate loaves into one unit for ḥalla?",
 "outcome": "not_dialectical",
 "outcomeNote": "a baraita records a three-way dispute without resolution",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "pesachim.48b.6",
   "daf": "48b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "תַּנְיָא, רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר אוֹמֵר: הַסַּל מְצָרְפָן. רַבִּי יְהוֹשֻׁעַ אוֹמֵר: תַּנּוּר מְצָרְפָן. רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר כִּכָּרוֹת שֶׁל בָּבֶל שֶׁנּוֹשְׁכוֹת זוֹ מִזּוֹ מִצְטָרְפוֹת.",
   "en": "«It was taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Eliezer says: A basket combines» different loaves placed in it with regard to the obligation to separate ḥalla. «Rabbi Yehoshua says: An oven combines them. Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says: Babylonian loaves that bite from one another are combined;» however, if the loaves are connected to any lesser degree, e.g., if they are together in an oven or basket, they are not considered combined for the purpose of separating ḥalla."
  }
 ],
